    "extracted text": "The ITH-zeotype germanosilicates were synthesized under hydrothermal conditions using TMHDA as an OSDA. In a typical synthesis, 4 mL of TMHDA and 0.0262 g GeO2 were added to 0.81 mL water. The mixture was stirred until the germanium oxide was dissolved. After adding 0.1 mL of TEOS, the mixture was stirred for 30 min at room temperature to hydrolyze the TEOS, followed by the addition of 0.057 mL of an aqueous HF solution. The molar ratio of the batch composition was 0.5GeO2:1SiO2:37.4OSDA:3HF:90H2O. The final mixture (pH 7–8) was sealed in a 25-mL Teflon-lined autoclave and heated to 170°C under autogenous pressure for 7 days. The solid product was recovered by filtration, washed with distilled water using ultrasonic cleaning, and dried overnight at 333 K. For the synthesis of Co- and Cu-containing ITH, CoCl2·6H2O and CuCl2·2H2O were used as the precursors, respectively, and added into the reaction gel to obtain the following molar composition: 0.5GeO2:1SiO2:37.4OSDA:3HF:90H2O:0.15CoO or 0.10 CuO.",
    
    "property mapping": "SiO2 = Si source (tetraethyl orthosilicate, TEOS)\nGeO2 = Ge source (germanium oxide)\nMeO = Metal oxide source (CuO or CoO from CuCl2·2H2O or CoCl2·6H2O)\nH2O = Water content\nTMHDA = N,N,N′,N′-tetramethyl-1,6-hexanediamine (organic structure-directing agent)\nHF = Hydrofluoric acid\nProducts = Resulting zeolite phase",
    
    "formula abbreviations": "TMHDA = N,N,N′,N′-tetramethyl-1,6-hexanediamine (organic structure-directing agent)\nMeO = Metal oxide, which refers to either CuO or CoO depending on the recipe\nITH = ITH-type zeolite framework\nTEOS = Tetraethyl orthosilicate (silicon source)",
    
    "ratio calculations": "For all recipes, I'm normalizing to Si = 1.0. \nFor SiO2/GeO2 ratios given as 1:0.5, Si = 1.0 and Ge = 0.5\nFor SiO2/GeO2 ratios given as 0.8:1, Si = 0.8 and Ge = 1.0, which normalizes to Si = 1.0 and Ge = 1.25\nFor SiO2/GeO2 given as 1:1, Si = 1.0 and Ge = 1.0\nFor SiO2/GeO2 given as 1:0.4, Si = 1.0 and Ge = 0.4\nFor SiO2/GeO2 given as 1:(0.1-1), taking the mean: Si = 1.0 and Ge = 0.55\nFor SiO2/GeO2 given as 0.8:0, Si = 1.0 and Ge = 0\nFor H2O ranges, I'm calculating the mean value (e.g., 15-90 becomes 52.5)\nFor TMHDA ranges, I'm calculating the mean value (e.g., 28.0-37.4 becomes 32.7)",
    
